    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0440" n="425" xml:id="pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 Recovery/9–2449</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by Mr. G. Hayden Raynor of
                        the United States Delegation at the United Nations</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-09-24">September 24, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Participants:</cell>
                        <cell>M. Maurice Couve de Murville, French Delegation</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Mr. G. Hayden Raynor, U.S. Delegation</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>During the course of Mr. Cohen’s<anchor n="1" xml:id="d249-f1"/> and my
                    conversation with Couve on the Greek matter, I inquired casually of Couve if
                    there had been any recent developments in Western Europe with respect to the
                    idea of Spaak heading up the OEEC Organization.</p>
                <p>Couve replied in almost these words: “What is the use of this now? Why should his
                    talents be wasted on this Organization now? The OEEC is dead. You have killed it
                    by your tri-partite financial talks in Washington.”<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d249-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d249-f1" n="1" xml:id="d249-f1-content">
                <p>Benjamin V. Cohen, an Alternate U.S. Representative at the United Nations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d249-f2" n="2" xml:id="d249-f2-content">
                <p>For documentation on these talks, see <ref target="#pg832">pp. 832</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
